---
import { age, number } from '../lib/data';
const { status, errors, forecast, ecmwf, gfs, rainfall, climate, pressure } = Astro.props;
const sources = [['Forecast / wind',forecast],['ECMWF ensemble',ecmwf],['GFS ensemble',gfs],['Rainfall history',rainfall],['Climate · ERA5',climate],['Pressure maps',pressure]];
---
<div class="section-line"><h2>Sources & collection status</h2></div>
<table><thead><tr><th>Saved source</th><th>Last collection</th></tr></thead><tbody>{sources.map(([name,value])=><tr><td>{name}</td><td>{age(value?.updated)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
<p class="note">Weather and city lookup: <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo · CC BY 4.0</a>. Model/reanalysis estimates, not local station readings. Page views and tab changes make no provider requests. Missing data remains unavailable.</p>
{status&&<table><caption>Recent usage · reservations, not upstream-reported counts</caption><thead><tr><th>UTC date / provider</th><th>Requests</th><th>Quota units</th><th>MiB</th></tr></thead><tbody>{status.usage.slice(0,4).map((u:any)=><tr><td>{u.day} · {u.provider}</td><td>{u.requests}</td><td>{number(u.units)}</td><td>{number(u.bytes/1048576,1)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>}
<p class="note">Shared caps: 24 HTTP attempts, 1,000 estimated quota units and 40 MiB per day. Open-Meteo’s published free allowance: 10,000 counted calls/day. No account/key is needed. Persistent caching, cooldowns and Retry-After apply; failures retain old data.</p>
{errors.length>0&&<p class="notice">{errors.length} collection issue(s). Run <code>make status</code> for saved errors and next eligible times.</p>}
